## 3. Pure BSEC Kinetics Architecture & iOS Integration

The **Pure BSEC Kinetics** sketch operates the sensor in continuous Low Power 3-second mode (`BSEC_SAMPLE_RATE_LP`) to keep the micro-heater plate continuously energized at ~300°C.

### Physical Formulas

1. **Gas Resistance Drop Percentage ($gDrop$):**

$$gDrop = \frac{R_{base} - R_{min}}{R_{base}} \times 100\%$$

2. **Moisture Delta ($\Delta RH$):**

$$\Delta RH = RH_{max} - RH_{base}$$

3. **$T_{50}$ Desorption Recovery Lag:** Time in seconds ($\tau_{50}$) for gas resistance to recover 50% from $R_{min}$ back toward $R_{base}$:

$$R_{target50} = R_{min} + 0.5 \times (R_{base} - R_{min})$$

* **Fast Recovery ($\tau_{50} < 3.5\text{s}$):** Non-sulfur organic molecules (beverage/food/alcohol esters) desorb rapidly.
* **Slow Recovery ($\tau_{50} \ge 3.5\text{s}$):** Volatile Sulfur Compounds ($H_2S$, methyl mercaptan) bind strongly to the plate.

### Refined Decision Matrix & Non-Judgmental App Mapping

| Result Code | $\Delta RH$ | $gDrop$ | $T_{50}$ Lag | iOS App Display Title | Physical Interpretation |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `BALANCED_BREATH` | $\ge 2.5\%$ | $< 15\%$ | **$< 3.5\text{s}$** | Fresh & Balanced Breath | Fresh baseline breath clearing rapidly |
| `SETTLE_BEVERAGE_FOOD_ODOR` | $\ge 2.5\%$ | $< 15\%$ | **$\ge 3.5\text{s}$** | Settling Flavor Notes | Trace organic residue settling post-ingestion |
| `SOME_BEVERAGE_FOOD_ODOR` | $\ge 2.5\%$ | $\ge 15\%$ | $< 3.5\text{s}$ | Food & Drink Aftertaste | Moderate non-sulfur organic residue |
| `NOTICEABLE_MALODOR` | $\ge 2.5\%$ | $15\% - 45\%$ | $\ge 3.5\text{s}$ | Freshness Boost Recommended | Moderate volatile sulfur compounds present |
| `STRONG_MALODOR` | $\ge 2.5\%$ | $\ge 45\%$ | $\ge 3.5\text{s}$ | Oral Hydration & Care Alert | High VSC concentration |
| `DRY_MOUTH_HYDRATE` | $< 2.5\%$ | $\ge 15\%$ | $< 3.5\text{s}$ | Hydration Boost Needed | Oral dehydration with food residue |
